# Rust
/target/
**/*.rs.bk
*.pdb

# Documentation site build output, and the Mermaid assets `mdbook-mermaid install book`
# generates. Both are produced by the Pages workflow; committing them would mean two sources of
# truth for a file nobody edits.
/book/book/
/book/mermaid.min.js
/book/mermaid-init.js

# Layover runtime state.
#
# Every directory, not just the repository root: `layover serve` writes `.layover/` next to
# whichever `layover.toml` it was pointed at, so running an example leaves state under
# `examples/…/.layover/`. That state is not inert — the journal holds queued flight bodies and
# help requests, and a help request is where an agent describes an authentication failure. A
# rooted pattern left all of it stageable by `git add -A`.
**/.layover/
**/workspace/

# Environment and secrets
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Editors and OS
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
